          "path": "_m/s/r/2/y/villa-borghese-gardens-wp/corner-of-villa-borghese.jpg",
          "filename": "Corner Of Villa Borghese.jpg",
          "caption": "Corner Of Villa Borghese.\nThe founder of the Villa, built in the early seventeenth century Cardinal Scipione, Cafarelli Borghese, nephew of Pope Paul V. Later, the Park was increased to 78 hectares. The tradition of the rest of the city has ancient origins. So rested in ancient Rome, Nero and Lucullus. The owners of the Villa sometimes opened the Park to the townspeople. This lasted until the era of major real estate speculation, which began in 1870, the King saved the Villa and the Park that first bought the Park, and then gave it to the residents of the city",
          "alt": "Corner Of Villa Borghese.\nThe founder of the Villa, built in the early seventeenth century Cardinal Scipione, Cafarelli Borghese, nephew of Pope Paul V. Later, the Park was increased to 78 hectares. The tradition of the rest of the city has ancient origins. So rested in ancient Rome, Nero and Lucullus. The owners of the Villa sometimes opened the Park to the townspeople. This lasted until the era of major real estate speculation, which began in 1870, the King saved the Villa and the Park that first bought the Park, and then gave it to the residents of the city",
